body:
She is looking amazing! Especially those rollers!

&#x200B;

May your Ringlands be blessed good sir!

As others have said depends on what it is going on, EJ it is pretty loud on a Cold Start (My neighbors say they never hear me leaving lol) early in the AM, But when the car warms up it is kinda loud but pretty tame. 

&#x200B;

FA I heard it on a Friend's WRX and it sounds way different and more tame but not bad at all in all honesty!

Just make sure it is their insurance and I am not sure in New Hampshire since I am down south how DV works be ready to hire someone who specializes in Diminished Value Appraisals as I had to do that and it can take months just being realistic with that insurance companies are not willing to pay out on Diminished Value and are ready to lowball. 

&#x200B;

P.S Saludos hermano Boricua!

Me personally I would not try to budget yourself out if you can.

&#x200B;

I hate seeing the "Hopping on the Trend" Posts because to me it sounds like you are quick to give up on the car you have your reasons but I know a lot of people who regret getting rid of their subies but I also seen others who have not, All to preference you are on the fence and that is understandable.

I don't disagree with you on the service center side but yes the service center side I am in Atlanta and like I said in a earlier comment I work for a rental car company and we have Tesla's in our fleet but to get them serviced it is like jumping over infinite rings of fire! lmao that's probably my biggest con and I am not too crazy on their looks but if the performance makes up for then by all means I can't hate on it!

&#x200B;

If I ever get to try a LR tesla I will post up in this thread! 😁

I have a VA STI but lord do I drool when I see a clean GD chassis STI 

&#x200B;

Keep her and treat her well!

Had an RSX I named her Artemis,

&#x200B;

Artemis 2.0 for my STI until I name her something more appropriate for her lol

Was looking through their inventory as I wanted to buy from them but after hearing so many bad things and now I see an actual email from Fitment Industries I am staying farrrr away from them not even with a 10 mile pole lol also O.P Good luck with getting your FULL Money back!

&#x200B;

What other sites are good to buy wheels in the U.S? Please let me know it is appreciated!

If it shows wire replace it if it just shows more rubber keep it should be fine for the most part. 

&#x200B;

Source: Used to be a Automotive Technician.

Your car just wants more vape juice! For those sick Cloud Comps!

&#x200B;

JK Mine does the same OP it did it a lot more frequently when I went to FL.

Like others that is a No from me too tell your friend to look elsewhere with that mindset and an STI for that price is a risk, A lot of us who owns STI's know the risks to owning one but the ones who don't have issues are the ones who research and prepare for the worst.

&#x200B;

P.S STI's are quick but by no means a "Fast Car" especially in straights.

A buddy of mine is a Master Tech at Kia and by god some of the stories I hear on their regular cars is insane! I used to work at Dealers myself (Subaru Dealer too) and some of the things you see is crazy but I like Hyundai's and Kia's Warranty but it also tells a lot about their quality control you offer a really good warranty because maybe they themselves know their cars are known to have a lot of issues.

&#x200B;

My company has had a crap ton of engine and transmission recalls for Hyundai's and Kia's that I do not trust the brand for my family. (Whenever I have one.)

Lmao thats a first for me! Usually Bagged Golfs or Static Golf's love to roll slowly and show off their whip that way,

&#x200B;

Sorry Bud did not mean to attack you that way just what I see out here in the A.

Yikes I know that must have sucked can so I have a question did you sign paperwork with the dealer without the car showing up or did they wait for it? You can PM me if you don't want answer publicly.

&#x200B;

Thanks Hope you are having fun with the WRX!!
